		"longform": ["High pH, smears wet and sets hard dry, poor emergence — that looks sodic. Gypsum is for alkali, not every white crust. Gypsum’s calcium swaps sodium, then water must wash sodium away. No drainage, wasted gypsum. Salt soils want leaching. Don’t gypsum an acid soil. On this patch, high pH is the first clue."],
